      {
        "id": 91336,
        "name": "Silverleaf",
        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-15T05:15:17.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Also saying that the game should be different is insulting to all the hardworking playtesters as well as the designers, implying that none of them did their job properly.</p><p>I for one am grateful to everyone involved in allowing me to play this, my favourite game ever. Thank you, I do appreciate it. Sure, in an ideal world I'd change a few minor things about it (mostly \"scanability\" of cards/effects), but I'd never tell a designer that they should have done something differently. (I might however ask about the thought process behind a particular decision or whether a certain situation came up in playtesting or similar, because it's extremely possible that I don't like something because I don't understand it properly.) I'm not a game designer and I don't presume to know better than <em>people who do this for a living</em>.</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:16:56.317Z",
