      {
        "id": 91337,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-15T05:30:45.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>I totally get people wanting to play the VV as individual villains.&nbsp; The Vengeance format can be a real hoot, but it also takes a lot of space.&nbsp; The format was incredibly different, however, and much of our playtesting efforts were dedicated to balancing it.&nbsp; I'd've been quite impressed if the VV could be played as individual decks and (H) decks as a balanced format, but between that and the heroes/environments it never was a subject that anyone really seriously attempt on top of everything else.<br><br>I definitely get people criticizing the <em>way</em> people criticize, but I'm all for criticizing.&nbsp; It tells &gt;G what people love, what they hate, and what they would like to see for the future.<br><br>Be brutal to the things you love, folks.&nbsp; It shows a lot of thought and care was put into what you have to say.&nbsp; Just makes sure you criticize <em>constructively</em> rather than incessantly.</p>",
        "post_number": 22,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:16:56.386Z",
