      {
        "id": 91339,
        "name": "Arcanist Lupus",
        "username": "Arcanist_Lupus",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arcanist_lupus/{size}/2169_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-15T06:13:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>And now I believe that THAT point has been emphasized effectively, and we should return to the origional topic of the thread which was, if I may summarize:<br><br>\"What would be the best way to house rule the V5 so that we could play against them individually\".</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Broccoli suggested playing H villian cards each turn, but was unsure how to multiply their health.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>One way to possibly determine health would be to play against them to exhaustion - i.e. play until all the heros are dead, and then record how much damage the villian took. &nbsp;Do this a dozen times and then average the score, and voila! &nbsp;(Note: &nbsp;I'm not sure this would actually work)</p>",
        "post_number": 24,
