      {
        "id": 91340,
        "name": "Reckless",
        "username": "Reckless",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/{size}/2467_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-02-15T06:23:19.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Well, we've only spent about a fifth of this page delving into the horror started by a poster using the word \"should\" in regard to Vengeance villain mechanics.&nbsp; I'm sure we can sprout off yet ANOTHER Off-Topic forum post on the nature of being angry at someone saying something we didn't like on the internet.<br><br>In other news, my group played a three player game against Fright Train during playtesting.&nbsp; I can't remember how different he was then compared to now, but it was as on ok game.&nbsp; I'd rank it as a quicker Ambuscade or Baron Blade game.&nbsp; A few (H) effects, more HP, and an interesting flip mechanic may do him some good.&nbsp; I'd see him redoubling his efforts after being reduced to 0 HP, so you could probably do a cool flip mechanic based on him being scuffed up and angry.&nbsp; You may not even need to raise his front side's HP by much.</p>",
        "post_number": 25,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T03:16:56.621Z",
